          "type": "heading",
          "text": "26. Which One To Reach For",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "List comp: two passes, indexing, or small data.",
            "Genexp: a single pass over big data.",
            "`sum`, `any`, `all`, `min`, `max` take genexps directly.",
            "So do `join`, `set`, and `dict` — no intermediate list."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`''.join([str(x) for x in it])` — join materializes anyway.",
            "`sum([...])` is the one that wastes real memory."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Scoping",
          "text": "Python 3 comprehensions own their scope, so the loop variable never leaks into the enclosing function. Python 2 leaked it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "27. yield Is An Expression"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "received = yield value  # value from caller",
            "g.send(x)   # yield -> x, returns next",
            "next(g)     # prime before any send"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`g.send(x)` resumes and makes the paused yield equal x.",
            "It returns the next yielded value, like `next()`.",
            "Prime a fresh generator with `next(g)` or `g.send(None)`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "28. Prime Or Crash",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Un-primed send: `TypeError: can't send non-None value`.",
            "A just-started generator has no paused yield to fill.",
            "The `@coroutine` decorator auto-advances on creation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def acc():",
            "    total = 0",
            "    while True: total += yield total",
            "a = acc(); next(a)   # prime",
            "a.send(10)           # 10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "29. throw and close",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`g.throw(Exc)` raises at the suspension point.",
            "The generator can catch and handle it there.",
            "`g.close()` raises `GeneratorExit` instead.",
            "Run cleanup, then let it propagate."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "next(g) prime",
              "send(x)",
              "yield → x",
              "close()",
              "GeneratorExit"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Uncaught `throw()` exception propagates to the caller.",
            "The generator is then CLOSED for good.",
            "Catching `GeneratorExit` and yielding → `RuntimeError`."
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Priming Decorators & Coroutine Lineage",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@coroutine",
            "def averager():",
            "    tot = n = 0; avg = None",
            "    while True:",
            "        tot += yield avg; n += 1",
